@nsobid-6830B3A12406CB4716FEC5ADDC35D3E2DC92D212

# Splatoon 3 11.2.0 - 1920x1080 resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Pins the game at 1920x1080 -- the resolution it already targets when docked.
//
// This is NOT a supersampling mod. It renders no more pixels than stock, costs
// no extra memory, and needs no DRAM Size change and no GPU-pool or heap patch;
// the stock 128 MB dynamic-texture pool is already sized for 1080p. The sead
// physical framebuffer is left alone for the same reason -- it is 1920x1080
// already.
//
// What it does is defeat dynamic resolution. Under load Splatoon 3 drops the
// render size down a built-in ladder (180, 360, 420, 480, 540, 600, 720, 900,
// 1080, 1440, 2160) and crops the presented image to match. This forces the
// ladder entry, the crop and the controller's full-resolution flag to 1080p, so
// the game holds full resolution instead of dipping.
//
// Use DOCKED mode (System > "Enable Docked Mode"); handheld sizes are stock.

@enabled
// Make the dynamic-resolution controller's apply path run on the first frame
// and publish this size to gfxstate+0x388, the field render targets are sized
// from. It normally fires only on an operation-mode change, which never happens
// when you boot straight into docked mode.
013638AC 08008052   // MOVZ W8,#0     (ctrl+0x320 cached op mode; was 1)
01363AE0 09878052   // MOVZ W9,#1080  (was ladder[idx])
01363B34 0AF08052   // MOVZ W10,#1920 (was FCVTZS W10,S0 = height/9*16)
// Drop that path's display-buffer crop write -- the display buffer does not
// exist yet on frame 1. The per-frame path below repeats it behind a null guard.
01363B44 1F2003D5   // NOP (was LDR  X11,[X11,#0x50]  = display buffer)
01363B48 1F2003D5   // NOP (was STRB W12,[X11,#0x52]  = crop dirty)
01363B4C 1F2003D5   // NOP (was STUR XZR,[X11,#0x54]  = crop x,y)
01363B50 1F2003D5   // NOP (was STP  W10,W9,[X11,#0x5C] = crop w,h)
// Force the controller's full-resolution flag (ctrl+0x31C) at both read sites,
// bypassing its per-frame min(ladder/height, 1.0) shrink.
01363B54 29008052   // MOVZ W9,#1
01363C08 2C008052   // MOVZ W12,#1
// Pin the two loads that feed nvnWindowSetCrop to the same size.
01363BFC 0AF08052   // MOVZ W10,#1920 (was LDR W10,[X11,#0x388])
01363C04 09878052   // MOVZ W9,#1080  (was LDR W9,[X11,#0x38C])
@stop

// Offsets reverse-engineered against Splatoon 3's sead + spl::gfx + agl/gsys
// engine; 11.2.0 retail is symbol-stripped, so every site was located by
// structure and byte-verified against the IDB.
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-patches
